    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. so like, if i'm looking at meal planning, what are some specific examples of high GI vs low GI foods? like for breakfast or lunch?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For breakfast, highly processed white bread or sugary cereals are high GI, whereas steel-cut oats or whole-grain toast are good low GI choices. At lunch, white pasta is high GI, but brown rice or quinoa are excellent low GI alternatives. Fruits like bananas are higher GI than berries, so incorporating a mix helps balance your meals. Always aim for complex carbohydrates rich in fiber to keep your GI low throughout the day.",
      "source": "target",
